WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:09.710
News stories predict a “retirement crisis”
of inadequate retirement savings.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.940
In response, progressives have proposed expanding
Social Security benefits and establishing

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.930
new retirement plans run by state governments.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.820
Americans are worried, and many pine for the
days of traditional pensions.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.850
But the data tell a very different story.

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.800
Far more Americans are saving in 401(k)s today
than ever had a traditional pension.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.190
Contributions as a percent of salaries have
risen by one-quarter since 401ks were introduced,

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.600
and total retirement savings have tripled.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:43.820
IRS data show that the typical retiree today
has an income higher than when he was working.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.329
Retirees are half as likely to live in poverty
as working-age households.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:51.260
And rather than running out of money, the
typical retiree’s net worth increases as

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.670
he gets older.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:56.560
The real crisis is in Social Security and
state and local government pensions, which

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.340
are underfunded by up to 26 trillion dollars.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.300
Sure, 401ks needs tweaks.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.750
But I’ll trust my retirement to the system
that’s working, not to government-run plans

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.280
that are short by trillions.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.660
What do you think about retirement savings?

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.020
Let us know in your comments.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:16.160
Also, let us know what other topics you’d
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.940
and be sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

